{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>You shall not pervert justice, and you shall not take a bribe.</b> Above, in the section of Mishpatim, He warned concerning the poor, and here without specification." "<b>And you shall not take a bribe.</b> Even without perverting justice, since He has already warned 'you shall not pervert justice.'" "<b>And it blinds.</b> An expression of distortion, like 'וסלף בוגדים ישדם' (and the distortion of the treacherous destroys them)." "<b>The words of the righteous.</b> They are the litigants, by analogy with 'והצדיקו את הצדיק' (and you shall acquit the righteous)."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:53:06.096293696Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}